{"id": "emergency-hotels-rooms-repairs-repayment", "title": "Emergency hotels: paid for the rooms, then for the repairs; federal repayment still short", "seconds": 157.7, "voice": "elevenlabs:iPYqcpY8j8Ap4jUf28I3", "narrator": "Michael", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "2cd439a17db7a23e", "words": 410, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "In 2020, San Francisco rented hotel rooms as shelter, under emergency buying rules.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.53, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Hotel rooms as shelter", "sub": "2020, emergency purchasing rules"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.4, 1.13, 1.38, 1.97, 2.27, 2.66, 2.94, 3.03, 3.81, 4.04, 4.56, 4.89]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[3]"], "text": "What did it cost? First, the rooms.", "t0": 5.65, "t1": 8.18, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "The rooms", "sub": "30 hotel payees, 31 agreements"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.3, 0.4, 1.32, 1.91, 2.06]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[3]"], "text": "297.6 million dollars.", "t0": 8.3, "t1": 11.23, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$297.6 million", "label": "to 30 hotel payees"}, "emph": ["297.6"], "wt": [0.0, 0.34, 0.73, 1.41, 1.68, 2.06, 2.44]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["oneLine", "amount", "established[1]"], "text": "Then came the repair bills. How much more?", "t0": 11.75, "t1": 14.97, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Then the repairs", "sub": "9 settlements"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.44, 0.54, 0.82, 1.48, 1.65, 1.85]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "established[1]"], "text": "44.5 million dollars.", "t0": 14.97, "t1": 17.11, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$44.5 million", "label": "in 9 damage settlements", "sub": "27% of what had been paid for those rooms"}, "emph": ["44.5"], "wt": [0.04, 0.7, 1.0, 1.35, 1.68]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "The biggest: Hotel Whitcomb.", "t0": 17.73, "t1": 19.41, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Hotel Whitcomb", "kicker": "The rooms", "sub": "459 rooms, fiscal 2020 to 2023", "chip": "$88.1 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.95, 1.3]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "88.1 million dollars for 459 rooms. Per room?", "t0": 19.53, "t1": 25.85, "shot": "b5", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "Hotel Whitcomb", "kicker": "The rooms", "sub": "459 rooms, fiscal 2020 to 2023", "chip": "$88.1 million"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.46, 0.78, 1.07, 1.43, 2.25, 2.45, 2.68, 2.93, 3.49, 4.9, 5.17]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "191,846 dollars.", "t0": 25.85, "t1": 29.1, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$191,846", "label": "per room, Hotel Whitcomb", "sub": "$177.52 a room a night, with meals and linen"}, "emph": ["191,846"], "wt": [0.04, 0.2, 0.53, 1.03, 1.58, 1.82, 2.14, 2.78]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Across 11 hotels,", "t0": 29.62, "t1": 31.48, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Total paid per room (11 hotels)", "rows": [["highest", "217374"], ["lowest", "68223"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.41, 0.75]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "68,223 to 217,374", "t0": 31.48, "t1": 37.73, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Total paid per room (11 hotels)", "rows": [["highest", "217374"], ["lowest", "68223"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.65, 1.4, 1.64, 2.01, 3.12, 3.28, 3.5, 3.88, 4.34, 5.08, 5.42, 5.8]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "dollars a room.", "t0": 37.73, "t1": 39.09, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Total paid per room (11 hotels)", "rows": [["highest", "217374"], ["lowest", "68223"]]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.74, 0.94]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what", "suspicious[0].why"], "text": "Compare that with leasing, or buying.", "t0": 39.21, "t1": 41.33, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Total paid per room (11 hotels)", "rows": [["highest", "217374"], ["lowest", "68223"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.54, 0.73, 1.4, 1.62]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Payments peaked at 115.6 million in fiscal 2021.", "t0": 41.45, "t1": 45.81, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Still paying", "kicker": "The rooms", "sub": "4 hotels in fiscal 2024 or later"}, "emph": ["115.6 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.78, 0.91, 1.07, 1.39, 1.85, 2.12, 2.44, 2.87, 3.06, 3.48, 3.77]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[0].what"], "text": "Four hotels were still being paid in 2024 or later.", "t0": 45.93, "t1": 49.46, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "calendar", "label": "Still paying", "kicker": "The rooms", "sub": "4 hotels in fiscal 2024 or later"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.92, 1.07, 1.35, 1.61, 1.92, 2.04, 2.35, 2.98, 3.19]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[8]"], "text": "Another, 685 Ellis, was paid 4.8 million as a shelter hotel,", "t0": 49.58, "t1": 56.19, "shot": "b8d", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "housing", "label": "685 Ellis", "sub": "paid $4.8 million as a shelter hotel"}, "emph": ["4.8 million"], "wt": [0.0, 1.04, 1.39, 1.89, 2.54, 3.37, 3.53, 3.79, 4.03, 4.28, 4.51, 5.04, 5.26, 5.32, 5.64]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[8]"], "text": "then bought for 19.9 million.", "t0": 56.19, "t1": 58.6, "shot": "b8e", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Then bought with State Homekey money", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "685 Ellis", "sub": "paid $4.8 million as a shelter hotel"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Bought for $19.9 million", "sub": "seller had held it 295 days"}, {"art": "money", "name": "State Homekey award", "sub": "$18.2 million"}]}, "emph": ["19.9 million"], "wt": [0.04, 0.24, 0.48, 0.64, 1.07, 1.39, 1.9]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[8]", "established[7]"], "text": "The seller had held it 295 days.", "t0": 58.72, "t1": 62.07, "shot": "b8e", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Then bought with State Homekey money", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "685 Ellis", "sub": "paid $4.8 million as a shelter hotel"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Bought for $19.9 million", "sub": "seller had held it 295 days"}, {"art": "money", "name": "State Homekey award", "sub": "$18.2 million"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.48, 0.63, 0.86, 0.98, 1.27, 1.67, 2.36]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["established[4]", "story[8]", "established[7]"], "text": "A State Homekey award of 18.2 million followed.", "t0": 62.07, "t1": 65.79, "shot": "b8e", "visual": {"type": "chain", "kicker": "Then bought with State Homekey money", "steps": [{"art": "housing", "name": "685 Ellis", "sub": "paid $4.8 million as a shelter hotel"}, {"art": "contract", "name": "Bought for $19.9 million", "sub": "seller had held it 295 days"}, {"art": "money", "name": "State Homekey award", "sub": "$18.2 million"}]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.21, 0.59, 1.04, 1.43, 1.6, 2.1, 2.38, 2.73, 3.24]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[1]"], "text": "Next, repairs. Why did the City pay for damage by guests?", "t0": 66.01, "t1": 70.48, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "contract", "label": "Damage settlements", "kicker": "The repairs", "sub": "22 December 2022 to 23 June 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.67, 2.05, 2.25, 2.35, 2.45, 2.67, 2.85, 2.99, 3.3, 3.47]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[1]"], "text": "Because the room deals made the City responsible for restoring each hotel.", "t0": 70.48, "t1": 74.08, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the City is responsible for all repair costs associated with restoring the hotel"}, "wt": [0.04, 0.38, 0.5, 0.78, 1.08, 1.25, 1.36, 1.63, 2.21, 2.35, 2.87, 3.11]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "established[1]"], "text": "Even past the contract’s limit.", "t0": 74.2, "t1": 75.72, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "the City is responsible for all repair costs associated with restoring the hotel"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.62, 0.72, 1.23]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The biggest: 19.5 million for the Whitcomb.", "t0": 75.84, "t1": 78.95, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19.5 million", "label": "Hotel Whitcomb settlement, $42,484 a room"}, "emph": ["19.5 million"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 1.16, 1.58, 1.83, 2.14, 2.53, 2.64, 2.74]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "Across the nine, 7.9 to 57 percent of what the rooms cost.", "t0": 79.07, "t1": 83.29, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$19.5 million", "label": "Hotel Whitcomb settlement, $42,484 a room"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.5, 1.18, 1.49, 1.75, 2.05, 2.15, 2.7, 3.11, 3.2, 3.35, 3.46, 3.77]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "The Board’s analyst had warned of it. So the question is why there was no cap.", "t0": 83.41, "t1": 87.56, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "why that liability had no ceiling"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.47, 0.85, 0.96, 1.21, 1.31, 2.09, 2.28, 2.39, 2.85, 2.97, 3.24, 3.38, 3.55, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "Last, repayment. The federal emergency agency pays back cities for disaster costs.", "t0": 87.78, "t1": 93.34, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Federal repayment", "kicker": "The repayment"}, "wt": [0.0, 1.07, 2.24, 2.39, 2.73, 3.2, 3.58, 3.88, 4.12, 4.43, 4.56, 5.04]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "About 91 percent was eligible, the analyst said. What’s on file?", "t0": 93.46, "t1": 98.12, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "Federal repayment", "kicker": "The repayment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.7, 1.03, 1.2, 1.78, 1.93, 2.26, 3.29, 3.56, 3.72]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[2]"], "text": "62.1 million dollars.", "t0": 98.12, "t1": 100.42, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$62.1 million", "label": "obligated for this kind of shelter", "sub": "21% of $297.6 million"}, "emph": ["62.1"], "wt": [0.04, 0.76, 1.06, 1.33, 1.74]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Why so little? Claims still under review aren’t in the federal file.", "t0": 100.94, "t1": 105.56, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "claims under review are not in it"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.53, 1.56, 2.0, 2.34, 2.58, 3.3, 3.68, 3.78, 3.88, 4.23]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why", "notEstablished[1]"], "text": "Until they’re decided, the City carries the cost.", "t0": 105.68, "t1": 108.46, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "claims under review are not in it"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.27, 0.45, 1.34, 1.51, 1.82, 2.18, 2.29]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "The agency’s appeal decisions on file don’t touch the hotels.", "t0": 108.58, "t1": 111.52, "shot": "b15a", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s7", "kicker": "FEMA second-appeal decisions, May and June 2026", "text": "$64,132 refused for portable toilets and sinks; neither concerns the shelter hotels", "mark": "$64,132"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.6, 0.91, 1.29, 1.43, 1.79, 2.03, 2.3, 2.4]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[0]"], "text": "Two refuse 64,132 dollars, for portable toilets.", "t0": 111.64, "t1": 115.9, "shot": "b15ax", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "s7", "kicker": "FEMA second-appeal decisions, May and June 2026", "text": "$64,132 refused for portable toilets and sinks; neither concerns the shelter hotels", "mark": "$64,132"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.29, 0.66, 1.19, 1.64, 1.81, 2.09, 2.54, 3.22, 3.38, 3.77]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "span", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "No project on file covers July 2020 to January 2021.", "t0": 116.02, "t1": 120.34, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "span", "from": "2020-07-01", "to": "2021-01-22", "days": "205", "fromLab": "gap begins", "toLab": "gap ends"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.6, 0.74, 1.08, 1.38, 1.75, 2.03, 2.65, 2.81, 3.42, 3.73]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "In fiscal 2023, federal grants came in 262.2 million short.", "t0": 120.46, "t1": 126.09, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$262.2 million", "label": "federal grant revenue short of budget, fiscal 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.22, 0.73, 1.04, 2.11, 2.49, 2.83, 3.07, 3.2, 3.5, 3.8, 4.39, 4.63, 4.89, 5.29]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "The agency put other places first.", "t0": 126.21, "t1": 127.93, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$262.2 million", "label": "federal grant revenue short of budget, fiscal 2023"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.59, 0.75, 0.94, 1.31]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "One more: what the City pays to settle claims", "t0": 128.15, "t1": 131.45, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["claims and judgments, fiscal 2019–2022", "$223.8 million"], "b": ["fiscal 2023–2026", "$333.9 million"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 1.11, 1.32, 1.43, 1.72, 2.1, 2.26, 2.55]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "rose from 223.8 million to 333.9 million.", "t0": 131.45, "t1": 137.32, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["claims and judgments, fiscal 2019–2022", "$223.8 million"], "b": ["fiscal 2023–2026", "$333.9 million"]}, "wt": [0.04, 0.31, 0.49, 0.73, 1.16, 1.83, 2.15, 2.4, 3.12, 3.27, 3.53, 3.87, 4.42, 4.77, 5.37]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3].what"], "text": "Most at the transit agency, to 72.8 million, and the utilities, to 71.7.", "t0": 137.44, "t1": 143.78, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Departments, fiscal 2023–2026", "rows": [["Municipal Transportation Agency", "72.8"], ["Public Utilities Commission", "71.7"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.42, 0.52, 0.61, 0.97, 1.75, 1.88, 2.38, 2.62, 2.84, 3.69, 3.88, 3.98, 5.05, 5.19, 5.72, 6.0]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]", "notEstablished[3]"], "text": "The records don’t show any hotel was overpaid, or any damage claim inflated.", "t0": 144.0, "t1": 147.96, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That any hotel was overpaid", "That any damage claim was inflated"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.45, 0.65, 0.89, 1.06, 1.37, 1.51, 2.54, 2.68, 2.85, 3.19, 3.46]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[2]", "next[3]"], "text": "What would settle it? The room deals, damage reports, and the City’s federal claims.", "t0": 148.08, "t1": 152.22, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "The room deals and the damage reports"}, {"who": "", "what": "The City’s federal claims list"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.33, 0.61, 1.02, 1.2, 1.45, 1.91, 2.24, 2.68, 2.82, 2.92, 3.28, 3.62]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Each deal was voted where a vote was required.", "t0": 152.34, "t1": 154.5, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.25, 0.49, 0.64, 0.93, 1.11, 1.19, 1.45, 1.62]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 154.62, "t1": 156.83, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.38, 0.77, 0.92, 1.18, 1.24, 1.33, 1.55, 1.8]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "The rooms · $297.6 million", "lead2": "The repairs · $44.5 million", "lead3": "The repayment · $62.1 million", "lead4": "Claims rising", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "midnight", "hook": "timeline"}